        "content": "# Quick Build: Add Json Validation\n\n**Created**: 2026-03-01T20:32:00Z\n**Request**: add a json validation script that's ultra performant\n**Scope**: Small\n\n## Plan\n\n**Reasoning**: This is an additive feature touching 2-3 new files in a single system (validation utility). No existing code needs modification beyond an optional package.json script entry. Risk is low since this is purely additive. Estimated effort is under 2 hours.\n**Files Affected**: `src/validate-json.ts`, `src/validate-json.test.ts`, `package.json`\n**Approach**: Create a high-performance JSON validation module using hand-written validation logic rather than heavy schema libraries. The validator will use early-exit strategies, avoid unnecessary allocations, and leverage TypeScript's type system for compile-time safety. It will expose a `validateJson` function that accepts a raw string and returns a typed result with error details. A companion test file will cover valid JSON, malformed JSON, edge cases (deeply nested, large payloads), and performance benchmarks. A `validate` script entry will be added to package.json for CLI invocation.\n**Estimated Effort**: 1.5 hours\n\n## Tasks\n\n- [ ] **T1**: Create `src/validate-json.ts` with a `validateJson(input: string)` function that performs fast structural validation using a single-pass character scanner with early bail-out on malformed input, returning a typed `ValidationResult` with success/error status and error position detail `[complexity:medium]`\n- [ ] **T2**: Add schema-based validation support via a lightweight `validateAgainstSchema(data: unknown, schema: JsonSchema)` function in the same module that validates parsed objects against a simple type/required/properties schema descriptor without pulling in external dependencies `[complexity:medium]`\n- [ ] **T3**: Create `src/validate-json.test.ts` with unit tests covering valid JSON strings, common malformation errors (trailing commas, unquoted keys, unclosed brackets), edge cases (empty objects/arrays, unicode, deeply nested structures), and schema validation cases `[complexity:simple]`\n- [ ] **T4**: Add a performance benchmark test that validates a large JSON payload (10k+ characters) and asserts sub-millisecond execution time for structural validation using `performance.now()` or Bun's built-in timing `[complexity:simple]`\n- [ ] **T5**: Add a `\"validate\"` script entry in `package.json` pointing to `bun run src/validate-json.ts` for CLI usage, and export the validation functions from `src/index.ts` if appropriate `[complexity:simple]`\n\n## Implementation Summary\n\n{To be added by task-builder}\n\n## Verification\n\n{To be added by task-reviewer if --review flag used}\n"
